  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 1230 AM MDT SUN OCT 25 2026\nThe seasonably cool and unsettled pattern will continue through the \nlong-term period. With zonal flow aloft offering multiple \nopportunity for shortwave passages. The next notable system will \napproach the area late this week, although uncertainty remains on \nexact location, magnitude, and timing. Precipitation chances will \nincrease Late Thursday into Friday to 20-60% (highest north and east \nof the Snake River Plain) as the low digs down into the northwest \n(which there is good ensemble agreement on). The question becomes \nwhether or not the low aloft rejoins the main flow or breaks off to \nthe south. The former of the two would keep showers over our area \nthrough Sunday, with the later offering a brief period of drying \ncome late Saturday before bringing more widespread precipitation \nSunday. With that uncertainty, elevated precipitation chances will \nbe carried through Sunday.",
